@startuml
' Transfer21.10 by Codex / Manager on explicit Owner instruction.
' Source 883b6d3a47f7113e44ede73c9ad16b40f15bbdaf:docs/project_management/change_plans/ui-chart-wheel/developer/sequence_diagrams/ui/005-accepted-once-editor.puml; no invented ADR approval.
' DRAFT Developer,20.10.2026; direct Owner A006 decision in Developer chat.
title DRAFT: submitted target, accepted-once reset and conditional editor collapse
autonumber
hide footbox
actor User
participant "main.mjs / draft" as Main
control "session.mjs" as Session
participant "Existing HTTP client" as HTTP
control "facts/chart_state" as Facts
User -> Main : explicit submit B, manual gate
Main -> Session : submit()
Session -> Session : capture immutable intent B / attempt / changed birth
Session -> HTTP : POST B
User -> Main : optional edit draft C while request pending
alt committed POST
  HTTP --> Session : valid committed ChartDTO
  Session -> Session : own_committed; consume live target once
else uncertain outcome
  HTTP --> Session : existing recovery outcome
  Session -> HTTP : existing bounded safe GET/bootstrap
  HTTP --> Session : current view
  Session -> Session : fresh matched live recovery target?
else already_applied
  HTTP --> Session : already_applied
  Session -> Session : mark live target as awaiting current confirmation
  Session -> HTTP : GET current
  HTTP --> Session : current view
  Session -> Session : fresh chart_ready and birth=B?
  note right of Session
  Confirm once as already_applied_target_confirmed.
  Source facts/summary remain GET; no producer provenance.
  Stale/different/failed does not consume the target.
  end note
end
Session -> Main : accepted view + new acceptanceSeq + policy
Main -> Facts : accepted facts + same acceptance envelope
Facts -> Facts : consume seq once; reset if confirmed changed birth; otherwise reconcile
Facts -> Facts : source index / HTML / passive SVG revision
Main -> Main : consume seq once
alt allowCollapse and current draft equals submitted B
  Main -> Main : collapse fields; move focus only if hiding focused editor control
else draft C
  Main -> Main : preserve open editor and draft C
end
Session -> HTTP : later explicit/foreground safe GET
HTTP --> Session : accepted current B
Session -> Main : new ordinary acceptance, reset=false / allowCollapse=false
Main -> Facts : preserve addressable selection and expansions
Main -> Main : keep user-opened editor; no second collapse
note over Main, HTTP
No automatic POST. Recovery/recheck and manual build remain reachable outside collapsed fields.
RESULT_SUPERSEDED is a distinct ordinary current cause; identity does not prove own goal.
end note
@enduml
